{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;It has not been demonstrated that the materials used\r\nin the facing flank elevations of the rear dormer, when viewed from ground\r\nlevel, would appear to be of similar colour and design to the materials used in\r\nthe main roof of the subject dwellinghouse. The proposed dormer would not\r\ntherefore be within the tolerances of Schedule 2, Part 1 Class B, Condition B.2\r\n(a) of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England)\r\nOrder 2015 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;It has not been demonstrated that the two rooflights\r\nin the front roof slope would not&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt; protrude more than\r\n0.15 metres beyond the plane of the slope of the original roof when measured\r\nfrom the perpendicular with the external surface of the original roof&lt;/span&gt;.\r\nIt would therefore not be within the tolerances of Schedule 2, Part 1 Class C,\r\nC1 (b).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal is NOT therefore a lawful development.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
